LAMMPS (22 Jul 2025 - Update 4)
  using 1 OpenMP thread(s) per MPI task
# Two-phase (solid-liquid) coexistence at ONE trial temperature T. Run from an element folder, one log per job:
#   lmp -in ../in.coexist.lmp -log log_<id>.lammps -var T 520 -var Tprep 505.1 -var Tmelt 1515.3 -var seed 2026
# Mirrors coolorbit/sim/melting.py (GB10, MACE) with a classical MEAM potential:
#   1. relax the crystal (NPT, anisotropic) at Tprep
#   2. freeze the lower half (z), melt the upper half at Tmelt with z free (the liquid's density differs from the
#      crystal's: lower for most metals, HIGHER for Ga and Bi, so z may shrink as well as grow)
#   3. quench the liquid half to T
#   4. production NPT (anisotropic, P = 0) at T; record PE/atom. Above Tm the liquid grows and PE rises;
#      below Tm the crystal grows and PE falls. analyze.py makes the call against the run's own noise.
# The thermostat of steps 2-3 measures ONLY the liquid half (compute tliq + fix_modify temp): by default fix npt
# on a group still computes T over all atoms, and with the frozen half at zero velocity the liquid would run at
# ~2x the set temperature.
# If the upper half did not melt (MELT_CHECK), this is single-phase heating in disguise: analyze.py refuses it.
# Never single-phase heating (superheats). Units: metal (ps, eV, A, bar).

variable        dt      index 0.002
variable        tdamp   index 0.1
variable        pdamp   index 1.0
variable        equil   index 4000
variable        melt    index 6000
variable        quench  index 3000
variable        prod    index 25000
variable        every   index 50
variable        validation index 0      # 1 = laptop validation run: analyze.py refuses it as a result

units           metal
atom_style      atomic
boundary        p p p
read_data       data.coexist.lmp
Reading data file ...
  orthogonal box = (0 0 0) to (29.16 29.16 60.458)
  1 by 1 by 1 MPI processor grid
  reading atoms ...
  1900 atoms
  read_data CPU = 0.002 seconds
include         potential.mod
# Sn: 2NN MEAM, NIST IPR 2018--Ko-W-S--Sn--LAMMPS--ipr1 (doi:10.3390/met8110900). Needs the MEAM package.
pair_style meam
pair_coeff * * potential/library.meam Sn potential/Sn.meam Sn
neighbor        1.0 bin
neigh_modify    every 1 delay 0 check yes
timestep        ${dt}
timestep        0.002

variable        pea equal pe/atoms
thermo_style    custom step temp pe ke press vol lx ly lz ecouple
thermo          ${every}
thermo          50

# 1. crystal at Tprep -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
velocity        all create ${Tprep} ${seed} mom yes rot no dist gaussian
velocity        all create 505.1 ${seed} mom yes rot no dist gaussian
velocity        all create 505.1 2026 mom yes rot no dist gaussian
fix             eq all npt temp ${Tprep} ${Tprep} ${tdamp} aniso 0.0 0.0 ${pdamp}
fix             eq all npt temp 505.1 ${Tprep} ${tdamp} aniso 0.0 0.0 ${pdamp}
fix             eq all npt temp 505.1 505.1 ${tdamp} aniso 0.0 0.0 ${pdamp}
fix             eq all npt temp 505.1 505.1 0.1 aniso 0.0 0.0 ${pdamp}
fix             eq all npt temp 505.1 505.1 0.1 aniso 0.0 0.0 1.0
run             ${equil}
run             4000
